y cared about  it and so guess what I stopped doing it  I eliminated it and so there's a lot of  things that you're probably doing that  you can just eliminate straight out the  next thing is to automate and you look  at the the things that you're doing  regularly and see is there a way that  you can have software or some other  technology do this for you on an autumn  basis anything that I'm doing on a  repeated basis I always try to look for  a tool to help me do it  faster better if you look at any kind of  software tool you know it makes fewer  mistakes it doesn't go on vacation  doesn't call in sick it doesn't give you  problems and so much better to automate  wherever you can and then the next one  is a delegate so the things that still  have to get done that you can automate  but shouldn't shouldn't be you doing it  you delegate you find somebody who can  do it for you either overseas remotely  or locally here as well and that helps  set up the system so that you can focus  on what highest value could bring your  company and when I go to work every day  I ask myself along the way what's the  most value that I can bring to my  business today and I look at the tasks  that I have laid out in front of me and  I'll consistently challenge them like  should I be doing this should I be doing  this at all and if if I should should it  be me doing this I understand my company  has to do this but it should it be me  who's doing instead of somebody on my  team or some way to automate it and so  it's a personal challenge that I ask  myself every day that may be helpful for  you so that that's the mindset that  comes from the 4-hour workweek the  e-myth is another great book that you  can check out and I have a list of my  favorite books off my blog it's over  chemical comm slash blog and there's a  list of my top 10 favorite books or if  you're on my newsletter you get that  list as well and both of those are on  there so the email talks a lot about the  systems and structure you need to set up  to create your business there's a lot of  worksheets that I've created if you go  to the website slash worksheets you'll  be to find all the worksheets that I  have on there that mail for most may  also help you a lot of those are general  so that the worksheets the 4-hour work  week the e-myth are very it's general  advice general business systems which is  extremely helpful you haven't done  anything before it'll change how you  think and make you much better business  owner from there you might want to also  look at whatever industry you're in I  didn't see what kind of business you're  running but also follow some of the  blogs and experts who cover your  industry so for example I'm in online  marketing and so I research and I follow  a lot of the bloggers who talk about  online mark  and I look at some of the things that  they write about and often they'll post  about their workflow and things they do  to be more productive some of the tools  that they use and very very industry  specific so what may be really helpful  for them may not be helpful for  everybody else but as somebody in that  industry it's really useful so I look at  different companies who are blogging in  your space  and also different experts who are  consultants or people who are hired guns  who blog in that space as well and  follow them and you'll learn specific  skills and processes that they may use  that you may not find in a book like the  4-hour workweek or my worksheets or the  email so those are my two suggestions  one look at those general resources  because that will change how you think  as a business owner and that will easily  apply over to any any kind of business  and that's why those books are really  successful and then I try to follow  experts who are in your industry who  might give you other specific ideas that  can help you even further automate and  and make your systems a lot better so  hopefully that helps congratulations on  taking the time t